    "problem_statement": "Unicode characters cause encoding errors when generating QR codes\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to generate QR codes with Unicode text, the library throws `UnicodeEncodeError: 'ascii' codec can't encode character` errors. This affects all image formats including PIL, SVG, and PNG output.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\n# This will fail with UnicodeEncodeError\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(\"Hello 世界\")  # Contains Unicode characters\nimg = qr.make_image()\n```\n\nThe error occurs when the library tries to process Unicode text data. Any non-ASCII characters in the input data will cause the encoding to fail.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe library should handle Unicode text properly and generate QR codes containing the Unicode data without encoding errors.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nUnicodeEncodeError: 'ascii' codec can't encode character '世' in position 6: ordinal not in range(128)\n```\n\nThis affects various use cases including:\n- International text in QR codes\n- Emoji characters\n- Any non-ASCII symbols\n\nThe issue appears to affect all image factory types (PIL, SVG, PNG) when Unicode data is provided."
